    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1366">

                <pb facs="0912" n="796" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg796"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/206.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Spanish Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spanish Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that my Government, to which I forwarded in due time the contents of
                    your excellency’s note of February 19th last<anchor n="115" xml:id="d1366-f1"/>
                    relative to the murder of the Spanish subjects Gonzalez brothers at Chihuahua,
                    instructs me to express its thanks for the attitude of the United States in the
                    case and, at the same time, to say to your excellency that it cherishes the hope
                    that your excellency will insist by all means at your disposal that a thorough
                    investigation of the facts be made by the Constitutionalist authorities.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Juan Riaño</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
